{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"ATTRIBUTION BOUNDARY, recorded so the census is checkable and because several failures were originally mis-attributed to the arms. Excluded as HARNESS faults, not tool faults: input asymmetry, where rebar read child and referenced tickets while other arms got the parent alone, 14 runs superseded and re-run; an extract.py non-greedy regex that read a complete 7-finding mini array as NO OUTPUT, which was one of the two Wave 3 mini interventions; my own subagent over-subscription, which triggered the superpowers inline fallback on js-gutenberg and contributed to CE persona losses on go-gitea; a resume message of mine that asserted children had returned and caused CE to synthesize from 5 of 7; acceptance-criteria scaffolding appended to rebar's input, which produced findings about the harness rather than the plan; and the supplement aggregator glob. RULE USED: a failure is the tool's when the tool had the information needed to avoid it or to report it. CE losing a persona is CE's, because CE knew the persona had not reported. The superpowers inline fallback is mixed - over-subscription triggered it, but only superpowers could have marked the artifact as degraded, and it did not."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789443142681206001,"uuid":"d403aab8-722a-4b11-ad5a-9ea59d29f034"}